    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d991">

                <pb facs="0950" n="938" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg938"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94114 Mail/62: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-17">April 17,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received April 17—10:54 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2423. American Interests, Japan. Department’s 435, February 9.<anchor n="27"
                        xml:id="d991-f1"/> Foreign Office note April 14 states Swiss Legation,
                    Tokyo, telegraphed <pb facs="0951" n="939" xml:id="pg939"/> April 13, it had
                    been advised by Japanese Foreign Office that commanders all internment camps
                        Japan<anchor n="28" xml:id="d991-f2"/> informed that POWs and civilian
                    internees should be permitted date correspondence.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[For memorandum dated April 18, prepared in the Office of Far Eastern
                        Affairs, discussing, among other subjects, “Efforts of this Government in
                        Behalf of American Prisoners of War and Civilian Internees in Japanese
                        Hands”, see <ref target="#pg1232">pages 1232</ref>, <ref target="#pg1234"
                            >1234</ref>.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d991-f1" n="27" xml:id="d991-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d991-f2" n="28" xml:id="d991-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 2830, May 4, the Minister in Switzerland stated that the words “and
                    Japanese occupied territory” should have been included after “Japan” (711.94114
                    Mail/75).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
